00:00:02.780 --> 00:00:05.180 align:start position:0%
the wastelands is a vast and dangerous  place one that you should ideally never  wander alone it thankfully you have the  option to bring a companion along for  the ride a friend to fight alongside and  someone to keep you company there are  over a dozen companions in Fallout 4  from a dog to a house robot to a cyborg  detective and a supermoon but what are  the benefits to having one well first of  all you can equip them with various  armors and weapons you find and also use  them as extra storage when you start to  get over encumbered you can instruct  your companions to move to different  locations to try to gain tactical  advantages as well as using them as bait  while you take cover to gain your health  back your companions can also help you  inspect objects and sometimes help you  hack a terminal or crack a safe if you  have the right one with you companions  can't be killed but they'll need  stimpaks and if they fall in combat you  have to use a stim pack to get them back  into the fight each companion acts  differently from the other and will  respond differently depending on how you  treat people or what you do in the  waistline to increase your affinity with  each companion you're going to have to  do something different let's take Nick  Valentine for example he likes it when  you hack terminals and when you treat  others with respect as you do this your  companion will like you more and more  each companion has his or her own unique  perks that will unlock once you've got  them to like you or possibly by  finishing and associated side quest for  that companion however if you do things  they don't like  you'll lose affinity with them then  they'll record on you but they'll start  to challenge you a bit more as you tell  them what to do so best to be on their  good side but which companions should  you take and where do you find them well  individual companions have strengths  some weaknesses  one of the first companions we'll run  into is dogmeat  we will find out the red rocket truck  stock he has a keen sense for searching  for things and will alert you when he's  found something or bring along your  trusty robot Butler codsworth who you'll  find back at sanctuary he isn't the  greatest offensively but he's loyal and  he won't let you down don't forget  pressing garvey who will give you some  nice range support with his laser musket  you'll meet them early in the main  storyline at the Museum of freedom  Piper who you'll find on your way into  Diamond City is surprisingly strong with  their pistol and if you can get her perk  you'll gain more XP from speed  challenges and finding new locations as  you progress through the main questline  you'll find Nick Valentine bring him  with you if you're not the most  intelligent person and need somebody to  do some hacking Kate is a nice companion  to have for close-quarters combat  because of a shotgun and she'll help you  pick locks if your skill isn't high  enough  you'll find her after you clear out the  combat zone if you're running into some  trouble with some tougher enemies and  you need some brute force bring along  strong the supermoon who has the ability  to carry more things than your normal  human you can find him at the Trinity  Towers give him a minigun and watch him  mow down your opposition there are more  companions to find but those are a few  without getting into too many spoilers  if you really want to enhance your  companions be sure to invest points into  charisma by leveling up the  inspirational perk your companions will  do more damage and they won't hurt you  if you level up attack dog Dogma can  bite and hold on to enemies giving you a  good opportunity to use your vats to  finish them up and that's a quick  rundown on companions in fallout 4 just  remember whoever you choose to take with  you on your waistline adventure make  sure you treat them right if you want to  get the best out of it and for more tips  on life in the wasteland stay tuned at  Gamescom and check out our fallout 4  show via the link on the screen below
 

